%S A239231 0,1,1,4,5,9,12,17,21,27,33,41,48,57,65,75,85,97,108,121,133,147,161,
%T A239231 177,192,209,225,243,261,281,300,321,341,363,385,409,432,457,481,507,
%U A239231 533,561,588,617,645,675,705,737,768,801,833,867,901,937,972,1009,1045
%N A239231 Heyawake numbers: maximum number of painted cells in an n X n grid, such that no two painted cells are orthogonally adjacent and the unpainted cells form a contiguous area.
%C A239231 Inspired by the Japanese puzzle of the same name.
%H A239231 Dmitry Kamenetsky, <a href="/A239231/a239231.txt">Optimal solutions for n <= 20 and 22 <= n <= 25</a>.
%H A239231 Dmitry Kamenetsky, <a href="https://puzzling.stackexchange.com/questions/141012/maximum-number-of-isolated-cells-on-the-8x8-grid">Maximum number of isolated cells on the 8x8 grid</a>, Puzzling StackExchange.
%H A239231 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heyawake">Heyawake</a>.
%H A239231 <a href="/index/Rec#order_08">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (2,-1,0,0,0,1,-2,1).
%F A239231 a(n) = floor(n^2/3) if n is even, a(n) = ceiling(n^2/3) if n!=3 is odd, as shown by Misha Lavrov's and Tom Sirgedas's answers to Dmitry Kamenetsky's question. - _Andrei Zabolotskii_, Oct 22 2026
%e A239231 For n=6, the painted cells could be A1, A3, A6, B5, C1, C3, D4, D6, E2, F1, F4, F6 (a(6)=12 cells in all):
%e A239231   #.#..#
%e A239231   ....#.
%e A239231   #.#...
%e A239231   ...#.#
%e A239231   .#....
%e A239231   #..#.#
%e A239231 For n=7, a(7) = 17:
%e A239231   #.#.#.#
%e A239231   .......
%e A239231   #.#.#.#
%e A239231   ...#...
%e A239231   #.#.#.#
%e A239231   .......
%e A239231   #.#.#.#
